  "markup": "\u003Ch3 style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ETop 3 Exercises for a Bigger Chest\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003EA well-developed chest is a hallmark of a strong, balanced physique. Whether you\u2019re chasing size, strength, or definition, focusing on key compound and isolation movements will get you there faster. Here are the top three exercises to help you build a bigger, fuller chest.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EKey Points\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EPrioritize \u003Cstrong\u003Econtrol\u003C/strong\u003E and a \u003Cstrong\u003Efull range of motion\u003C/strong\u003E over heavy, sloppy reps.\u003Cbr\u003EAdd a \u003Cstrong\u003Epause\u003C/strong\u003E where tension is highest to get more from every contraction.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EProgress weekly\u003C/strong\u003E \u2014 weight, reps, or total volume.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EBalance pressing\u003C/strong\u003E with rows or face pulls to protect your shoulders.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E1. Incline Barbell Bench Press\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EThe incline bench press targets your \u003Cstrong\u003Eupper chest\u003C/strong\u003E, adding that sought-after fullness near the collarbone.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E\u003Cem\u003EHow to do it:\u003C/em\u003E\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003ESet your bench to a \u003Cstrong\u003E30\u201345\u00B0\u003C/strong\u003E angle and retract your shoulder blades.\u003Cbr\u003EGrip the bar \u003Cstrong\u003Eslightly wider than shoulder width\u003C/strong\u003E and lower under control to your upper chest.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPress\u003C/strong\u003E back up, keeping your chest high and forearms vertical.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E\u003Cem\u003ETip:\u003C/em\u003E\u003C/strong\u003E Don\u2019t overload the bar \u2014 controlled reps protect shoulders and boost pec activation.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E2. Cable Flyes\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003ECable flyes provide \u003Cstrong\u003Econstant tension\u003C/strong\u003E throughout the movement, helping define and shape your pecs.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E\u003Cem\u003EHow to do it:\u003C/em\u003E\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003ESet pulleys around \u003Cstrong\u003Eshoulder height\u003C/strong\u003E with a slight forward lean and soft elbow bend.\u003Cbr\u003EBring your hands together and \u003Cstrong\u003Esqueeze 1\u20132 seconds\u003C/strong\u003E at the peak.\u003Cbr\u003EReturn slowly to the start without letting the shoulders roll forward.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E\u003Cem\u003ETip:\u003C/em\u003E\u003C/strong\u003E High-to-low hits the lower chest; low-to-high targets the upper chest; mid height works the mid-pecs.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E3. Dips\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EDips are a powerhouse for building \u003Cstrong\u003Elower-chest thickness\u003C/strong\u003E and \u003Cstrong\u003Etriceps strength\u003C/strong\u003E. Done correctly, they add both size and pressing power.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E\u003Cem\u003EHow to do it:\u003C/em\u003E\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003EUse parallel bars and \u003Cstrong\u003Elean slightly forward\u003C/strong\u003E to bias the chest.\u003Cbr\u003ELower to about \u003Cstrong\u003E90\u00B0\u003C/strong\u003E at the elbows, keeping shoulders down and back.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPress through the palms\u003C/strong\u003E, maintaining chest tension.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E\u003Cem\u003ETip:\u003C/em\u003E \u003C/strong\u003EAdd a dip belt for progressive overload once bodyweight dips are comfortable.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EProgramming Tips\u003C/strong\u003E\u003Cbr\u003ETrain chest \u003Cstrong\u003E2\u00D7 per week\u003C/strong\u003E \u2014 one heavier session and one focused on volume/pump.\u003Cbr\u003EAim for \u003Cstrong\u003E8\u201315 total working sets\u003C/strong\u003E per week across presses and flyes.\u003Cbr\u003ETrack progress and increase \u003Cstrong\u003Eload, reps, or tempo\u003C/strong\u003E gradually each week.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
      <Value Culture="sv"><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
